          "duration_s": 11.107199999999999,
          "headline": "Delphi · Lean for biology",
          "id": "commons",
          "narration": "Delphi is building toward Lean for biology: a shared foundation of biological mathematics that people and machines can inspect.",
          "start_s": 0.0
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 11.467199999999998,
          "headline": "Claims carry assumptions and evidence",
          "id": "claim",
          "narration": "Formalize the claim, its assumptions and its evidence. Then reuse that knowledge to solve constraints and explore new designs.",
          "start_s": 11.107199999999999
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 8.4072,
          "headline": "A checked theorem with a scope",
          "id": "proof",
          "narration": "In Frontier, Lean compiled a fin-beam theorem and rejected a corrupted law.",
          "start_s": 22.574399999999997
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 10.8912,
          "headline": "A biological compiler is the ambition",
          "id": "design",
          "narration": "A flying-fish design shows the ambition: connect genes, growth, mechanics and behavior into a biological compiler.",
          "start_s": 30.981599999999997
        },
        {
          "duration_s": 18.127200000000002,
          "headline": "Build a shared research commons",
          "id": "community",
          "narration": "Its intended output is candidate DNA, a build plan and validation tests. Through an open MCP interface, contributors can share results, challenge claims and advance the next question together.",
          "start_s": 41.8728
        }
      ],
      "title": "Delphi · one-minute vision cut"
